From aeddabc3b6b04424d48e43c3e635c0f82572ad47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:00:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, acp_thread: the ring's quota rows refresh live and
 say so
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.16 (ask 36). Hovering the context ring asked
Claude Agent (Plus) for the account quota at most once every 5 s, and
the tooltip showed the cached rows with no sign of what they were, so
the Weekly bar looked late. Three changes:

- The hover interval is 1 s. The agent's shared sample (5 s in plus)
  already absorbs a tighter loop, so this costs no extra report.
- A click on the ring asks even inside that interval, for a pointer
  that cannot hover. A request in flight still absorbs it.
- A line under the quota rows says what they are: "Refreshing…" while
  the agent answers, "Updated at HH:MM:SS" (local time) once a window
  arrives -- an unchanged window too, so the time moves -- and
  "Refreshes when the turn ends" while a turn runs.

Nothing is asked during a turn. Plus answers `refreshed: false` then on
purpose: SDK control requests are serialized, and an interrupt queued
behind a usage request would delay Stop. Asking only cost a round
trip; the turn's own end refreshes the rows.

The tooltip now reads the quota rows when it is built, not when the
ring was drawn. It opens after the hover delay, and the refresh the
hover asked for usually lands inside that delay, so rows captured at
render time showed the previous sample, with no later notification to
correct them. Measured on Xvfb against a stub agent: the agent sent
43% on the hover and 44% on the click, and the tooltip drew 42% and
43%; with the fix, 43% and 44%.

AcpThread gains account_usage_refresh_status() and a `force` argument
on refresh_account_usage. The tooltip reads the status where it already
re-reads the rows.

Tests, each seen failing first against stubs:
acp_thread_account_refresh_tests.rs (a click skips the interval but not
a request in flight; a hover asks again after 1 s; Refreshing then
Updated; nothing asked during a turn, AfterTurn until it ends) and
thread_view/tests/account_refresh_line_tests.rs (the line's wording).
---

